{"name":"Chive Flower","hex":"#a193bf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial plant, Allium schoenoprasum, related to the onion.","The leaves of this plant used as a herb."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece cut off; sliver.","The filament which supports the anther of a flower; stamen, especially of saffron."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chive"},{"term":"flower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorful, conspicuous structure associated with angiosperms, frequently scented and attracting various insects, and which may or may not be used for sexual reproduction.","A reproductive structure in angiosperms (flowering plants), often conspicuously colourful and typically including sepals, petals, and either or both stamens and/or a pistil."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put forth blooms.","To decorate with pictures of flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Allium tuberosum","blocks":[{"text":"Allium tuberosum is a species of plant native to the Chinese province of Shanxi, and cultivated and naturalized elsewhere in Asia and around the world. It has a number of uses in Asian cuisine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Allium_tuberosum_kz01.jpg/330px-Allium_tuberosum_kz01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allium_tuberosum","wikidata":"Q42285"},{"title":"Chives","blocks":[{"text":"Chives, scientific name Allium schoenoprasum, is a species of flowering plant in the family Amaryllidaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Allium_schoenoprasum_-_Bombus_lapidarius_-_Tootsi.jpg/330px-Allium_schoenoprasum_-_Bombus_lapidarius_-_Tootsi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chives","wikidata":"Q51148"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower","wikidata":"Q506"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Garlic_chives_1.jpg/500px-Garlic_chives_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Garlic_chives_1.jpg/1280px-Garlic_chives_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Garlic_chives_1.jpg/500px-Garlic_chives_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGarlic_chives_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/HK_%E6%B7%B1%E6%B0%B4%E5%9F%97_Sham_Shui_Po_104_%E7%A6%8F%E8%8F%AF%E8%A1%97_Fuk_Wa_Street_%E5%9C%93%E6%96%B9%E9%A4%83%E5%AD%90%E7%B2%A5%E9%BA%B5_Yuen_Fong_restaurant_green_%E9%9F%AE%E8%8F%9C_Allium_tuberosum_Dec_2018_SSG_01.jpg/500px-HK_%E6%B7%B1%E6%B0%B4%E5%9F%97_Sham_Shui_Po_104_%E7%A6%8F%E8%8F%AF%E8%A1%97_Fuk_Wa_Street_%E5%9C%93%E6%96%B9%E9%A4%83%E5%AD%90%E7%B2%A5%E9%BA%B5_Yuen_Fong_restaurant_green_%E9%9F%AE%E8%8F%9C_Allium_tuberosum_Dec_2018_